------------- NVBit (NVidia Binary Instrumentation Tool v1.8.1) Loaded --------------
NVBit core environment variables (mostly for nvbit-devs):
ACK_CTX_INIT_LIMITATION = 0 - if set, no warning will be printed for nvbit_at_ctx_init()
            NVDISASM = /usr/local/cuda-13.2/bin/nvdisasm - override default nvdisasm found in PATH
            NOBANNER = 0 - if set, does not print this banner
       NO_EAGER_LOAD = 1 - lazy module loading is now turned on by default. If you see deadlocks in your tool, set NO_EAGER_LOAD to 0
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
         INSTR_BEGIN = 0 - Beginning of the instruction interval where to apply instrumentation
           INSTR_END = 4294967295 - End of the instruction interval where to apply instrumentation
    EXCLUDE_PRED_OFF = 1 - Exclude predicated off instruction from count
DYNAMIC_KERNEL_LIMIT_END = 0 - Limit of the number kernel to be printed, 0 means no limit
DYNAMIC_KERNEL_LIMIT_START = 0 - start to report kernel from this kernel id, 0 means starts from the beginning, i.e. first kernel
   ACTIVE_FROM_START = 1 - Start instruction tracing from start or wait for cuProfilerStart and cuProfilerStop. If set to 0, DYNAMIC_KERNEL_LIMIT options have no effect
        TOOL_VERBOSE = 0 - Enable verbosity inside the tool
INTERMEDIATE_EXTRA_FILES_PERSISTANCE = 0 - Enable to not delete intermediate files from the extra trace generation
SKIP_ENHANCED_TRACER = 1 - Skip the post-execution enhanced_tracer pass (cubin extraction + parse_sass + parse_rfu). Primary trace artifacts (dynamic_trace.pb, per-CTA pb files, stats.csv) are unaffected.
ENHANCED_TRACER_PER_CUBIN_TIMEOUT_S = 30 - Per-subprocess deadline (seconds) for the cuobjdump/nvdisasm shell-outs inside enhanced_tracer. On timeout the child process group is SIGTERM'd then SIGKILL'd; the parent always returns normally. Set to 0 to wait indefinitely (legacy behavior).
ENHANCED_TRACER_MAX_PARSER_INPUT_KB = 64 - Maximum size (KB) of the .sass / .rfu files passed to parse_sass / parse_rfu. Cubins whose generated parser inputs exceed the threshold (or whose subprocess timed out) are skipped with a typed enhanced_tracer_cubin_parse_timeout diagnostic. Set to 0 to disable the size pre-skip.
     TOOL_TRACE_CORE = 0 - write the core id in the traces
TERMINATE_UPON_LIMIT = 0 - Stop the process once the current kernel > DYNAMIC_KERNEL_LIMIT_END
USER_DEFINED_FOLDERS = 1 - Uses the user defined folder TRACES_FOLDER path environment

 Traces location is /root/sm120_rtx_5090_capture/captures/simbench_l1_global_scalar_32b_copy/ 
Stats location is /root/sm120_rtx_5090_capture/captures/simbench_l1_global_scalar_32b_copy/stats.csv 
 TRACE_SAMPLING_MODE = 0 - Trace-sampling capture mode: 0=off, 1=counting-only (per-block stats, no address payload), 2=selective-dump (write only the TRACE_SAMPLING_SELECTED_BLOCKS whole blocks; counting stays on)
THRESHOLD_UNIQUE_KERNEL_CHECKING = 10 - Number of instructions used to check if kernels with the same name are different
    GATHER_REGISTERS = 0 - Compatibility knob; protobuf register snapshots are not emitted by this tracer.
